  "content": "[Intro]\n[Aadd9]\n[E/A]\n[Em/A]\n[Asus2add13]\n[Dmadd9/A]\n[A]\n[Dm6]\n[E7]If a\n\n[Verse 1]\n[Aadd9]picture paints a thou-\n[E/A]sand words, Then why\n[Em/A]can't I paint you?\n[Asus2add13]The words\n[Dmadd9/A]will never show\n[A]the you\n[Dm6]I've come to know.\n[E7]If a\n[Aadd9]face could launch a thou-\n[E/A]sand ships, Then\n[Em/A]where am I to\n[Asus2add13]go? There's no\n[Dmadd9/A]one home but you,\n[A]You're all\n[Dm6]that's left me to.\n[E7]And when\n\n[Chorus]\n[F#m]my love\n[F#m/F]for life\n[A6/E]is running dry,\n[D6]You\n[Em/C#]come and pour\n[F#7]your-\n[Bm7]self on\n[E7]me. If a\n\n[Verse 2]\n[Aadd9]man could be two pla-\n[E/A]ces at one time,\n[Em/A]I'd be with you.\n[Asus2add13]Tomor-\n[Dmadd9/A]row and today,\n[A]beside\n[Dm6]you all the way.\n[E7]If the\n[Aadd9]world should stop revol-\n[E/A]ving spinning slow-\n[Em/A]ly down to die,\n[Asus2add13]I'd\n[Dmadd9/A]spend the end with you.\n[A]And when\n[Dm6]the world was through,\n[E7]Then\n\n[Chorus]\n[F#m]one by one\n[F#m/F]the stars\n[A6/E]would all go out,\n[D6]Then\n[Em/C#]you and I\n[F#7]would\n[Bm7]simply\n[E7]fly a-\n\n[Outro]\n[Aadd9]way\n[Bm7add11/A]\n[Dmadd9/A]\n[A]",
